<title>USA: EU, U.S. in joint complaint against Japan - WSJ.</title>
<headline>EU, U.S. in joint complaint against Japan - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will likely announce on Wednesday that it will join the United States in its trade complaint against Japan and Fuji Photo Film Co Ltd, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The newspaper cited European Commission sources in its Wednesday edition as saying the union would make its announcement in Geneva.</p>
<p>Eastman Kodak Co and the United States are complaining before the World Trade Organization that Japan is restricting foreign access to its film and photographic paper markets.</p>
<p>The newspaper said U.S. and Japanese officials said they did not know of the union's decision to support the trade complaint.</p>
</text>
